  "query_preview": "..\n\nNext 7 days (through Wednesday)...\n\nHigh amplitude ridge axis right over our region today will slide \nslowly east as a splitting trough pattern moves into the Rockies \ntonight into Friday. Mid level winds will back to the \nsouth/southwest over the area by Friday. The surface pressure \ngradient will tighten across our eastern plains in response. Look \nfor brisk southeast winds across our eastern border counties \n(Custer, Fallon, Powder River, Carter) with gusts 30-45 mph \npossible. Breezy conditions are also possible in the Beartooth \nfoothills and Livingston vicinity (gusts 25-35 mph) at times.\n\nAs the split flow trough moves across the Rockies on to the \nplains Saturday/Saturday night, we expect just a few rain/snow \nshowers over the higher terrain of the Beartooths/Absarokas with \nsome virga possible over the nearby plains. Otherwise, dry \nconditions are expected through at least Monday night. Ensembles \nare suggesting a possible pattern change to cooler and unsettled \nweather by Tuesday/Wednesday of next week. However, there is a \nwide spread of possibilities and thus high uncertainty regarding \nhow the pattern unfolds. For now, we will carry scattered PoPs \nmoving into the mountains by Tuesday and spreading to the plains \nby Wednesday with a cooling trend. \n\nAs for temps...Above normal temperatures will prevail through the\nweekend, mainly in the mid 50s and 60s. Temps will cool to the \n50s Monday before dropping into the 40s by Wednesday. Overnight \nlows will be mainly 30s and 40s. BT",
